"t71s_secasl":{"history_id":16466157,"link":"https://www.pangram.com/history/8f47ecd9-5196-4eed-b179-bde28cd51324","utc":"2026-10-18T04:10:13Z","words":1442,"avg_ai_likelihood":0.15767066180706024,"headline":"AI Detected","version":"4.0","windows":["Human, High, 104","AI-Generated, High, 52","Human, High, 77","AI-Generated, High, 200","Human, High, 1009"],"flagged":["AI-Generated (52 words): Remember those guards from the urge to escape? Same deal here, so get enough Nurturer and Protector in the room before you go deep. Borrowed is fine, as long as it's from someone steady who won't try to run your trip for you. And yes, those caution signs still count.","AI-Generated (200 words): Keep it as a reference point, no need to keep chasing it. Feeling it once is a long way from feeling it only when you're tripping, and that's still a long way from feeling it on a regular morning while the coffee brews.\nCareful, though, because that night can turn into a hook. Suddenly it's the bar. Every plain old morning with the coffee feels like failing next to it. Does a trip that big mean what you saw really happened, or that you're done healing? Not necessarily. It can be gorgeous and still mean neither. What I'd watch is the weeks after. Are you a bit more honest, more protective of your little one, more reliable, all that?\nAnd what if your little one still can't take the love in? Then don't go bigger. A stronger trip, a longer session, one more push for a breakthrough, all that just piles more on a little one who can't take in what's already there. Something's in the way of the love, so meet that first. Maybe a protective part doesn't trust it yet (and honestly, it might have its reasons)."]},
